    <script type="application/ld+json">{"mainEntity":{"headline":"eDNA insights and macroinvertebrate biomonitoring: a review of current practices and future directions for freshwater ecosystem assessment","description":"This review examines the integration of environmental DNA (eDNA) technology with macroinvertebrate biomonitoring for freshwater biodiversity and ecosystem assessment. Traditional macroinvertebrate monitoring provides well-established indicators of ecosystem health and water quality but can be resource-intensive and may have limitations in detecting rare, cryptic, or morphologically difficult taxa. eDNA offers a noninvasive molecular approach for detecting genetic material released by organisms into the environment and can expand the taxonomic breadth and scalability of biodiversity assessment. This review evaluates eDNA alongside conventional approaches, highlighting advances in sample collection, DNA extraction, quantitative polymerase chain reaction (qPCR), metabarcoding, and next-generation sequencing, while addressing challenges associated with DNA degradation and transport, primer bias, incomplete reference databases, contamination, and data interpretation. Although eDNA provides important advantages for biodiversity detection, its performance depends on sampling strategy, molecular protocols, reference-database completeness, and bioinformatic procedures; therefore, it should currently be regarded as complementary to, rather than a universal replacement for, conventional freshwater macroinvertebrate surveys. The review emphasizes the need for standardized eDNA protocols, expansion and curation of genetic reference databases, validation against established biomonitoring methods, and integration of molecular data with conventional surveys and ecological indices. The novelty of this review lies in combining technical evaluation, methodological recommendations, and integration strategies to support more comprehensive, reliable, and scalable freshwater biodiversity monitoring and ecosystem management.","datePublished":"2026-09-24T00:00:00Z","dateModified":"2026-09-24T00:00:00Z","pageStart":"1","pageEnd":"22","sameAs":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00027-026-01365-5","keywords":["Biomonitoring","Aquatic macroinvertebrate","DNA metabarcoding","DNA barcoding","Bioinformatics","Freshwater & Marine Ecology","Marine & Freshwater Sciences","Oceanography","Ecology","Life Sciences","general","Environmental Management"],"image":["https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00027-026-01365-5/MediaObjects/27_2026_1365_Figa_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00027-026-01365-5/MediaObjects/27_2026_1365_Fig1_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00027-026-01365-5/MediaObjects/27_2026_1365_Fig2_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00027-026-01365-5/MediaObjects/27_2026_1365_Fig3_HTML.png","https://media.springernature.com/lw1200/springer-static/image/art%3A10.1007%2Fs00027-026-01365-5/MediaObjects/27_2026_1365_Fig4_HTML.png"],"isPartOf":{"name":"Aquatic Sciences","issn":["1420-9055","1015-1621"],"volumeNumber":"88","@type":["Periodical","PublicationVolume"]},"publisher":{"name":"Springer International Publishing","logo":{"url":"https://www.springernature.com/app-sn/public/images/logo-springernature.png","@type":"ImageObject"},"@type":"Organization"},"author":[{"name":"Noran M. Tawfik","affiliation":[{"name":"Suez Canal University","address":{"name":"Department of Zoology, Faculty of Science, Suez Canal University, Ismailia, Egypt","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Nahla S. El-Shenawy","affiliation":[{"name":"Suez Canal University","address":{"name":"Department of Zoology, Faculty of Science, Suez Canal University, Ismailia, Egypt","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Rowaida Saleh Ahmed","affiliation":[{"name":"University of Saskatchewan","address":{"name":"Toxicology Centre School of Environmental Sustainability, University of Saskatchewan, Saskatoon, Canada","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"@type":"Person"},{"name":"Marwa I. Saad El-Din","affiliation":[{"name":"Suez Canal University","address":{"name":"Department of Zoology, Faculty of Science, Suez Canal University, Ismailia, Egypt","@type":"PostalAddress"},"@type":"Organization"}],"email":"marwasaadeldin88@gmail.com","@type":"Person"}],"isAccessibleForFree":false,"hasPart":{"isAccessibleForFree":false,"cssSelector":".main-content","@type":"WebPageElement"},"@type":"ScholarlyArticle"},"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"WebPage"}</script>

        
        
